b['stone_audit'] = 'Stone’s express reverse/remand core joins the complete continuing-authority rationale and preserved eligibility/remand conditions. The statutory duty remains mandatory. The draft distinguishes Bean, applies Ventura only to a still-unperformed initial agency factual task with its compelled-result qualification, and preserves Sigmon’s complete relevant category limits. His independently supported delay-remedy reservation is retained without creating a new delay claim. No fallback or new alternative ground is used.'
b['compatibility'] = 'The final six-Justice rationale consists of Stone’s approved position and Stevens, Kennedy, Souter, Ginsburg, and Breyer’s reconciled commitments. O’Connor’s original provisional reversal is superseded by the express frozen reconciliation, which supports affirmance with Scalia and Thomas on the combined date, source, baseline, and correction structure. No drafting change converts any of those three to the majority. Scalia authors the shared contextual objection because his frozen formulation develops those exact provisions; this is an assembly choice based on the frozen position, not an imported historical assignment. Thomas’s emphasis on the mandatory language is represented in that joined dissent and does not require a redundant separate writing. The full accounting objection and Brock’s contextual qualification are answered. No material historical departure remains after reconciliation.'
