metadata = []
for case in cases:
    public = {
        'Event':case['event'],
        'Participation':'Chief Justice Stone-Zsela and Justices Stevens, O’Connor, Scalia, Kennedy, Souter, Thomas, Ginsburg, and Breyer participated at argument and decision.',
        'Public Action':case['result'],
        'Judgment & Remedy':case['judgment'],
        'Opinion Topology':case['topology'],
        'Holdings':case['holdings'],
        'Precedent Treatment':case['precedent'],
        'Law After Decision':case['law'],
        'Separate Writings':case['separates'],
        'Procedure After Action':case['procedure'],
        'Source Notes':case['sources'],
    }
    internal_opinion_table = case['topology']
    if case['number'] in [30,34]:
        internal_opinion_table += '\n\n| Writing | Author | Joined by | Scope |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Opinion of the Court | @@LEAD@@ | @@LEAD_JOINERS@@ | Entire opinion and each judgment component. |'
        if case['number']==34:
            internal_opinion_table += '\n| Dissent | Scalia | O’Connor, Thomas | Contextual expiration ground and consolidated affirmance. |'
    internal = f'''**Case and dockets:** {case['case']}; {case['dockets']}.
**Event and date:** Merits decision; {case['date']}; October Term 2002, chunk 3.
**Result:** {case['result']}
**Version / lineage:** Original decision.

## Event, posture, and chronology

{case['event']}

The authorized neutral packet supplies the historical lower-court posture, factual limits, and requested relief. The event date follows the supplied term schedule; the argument date is supported by the saved primary syllabus. The supplied posture is properly before the Court, subject to Guillen’s actual component-finality question. No historical post-divergence grant or vote is independently admitted. Same-date cases use the same antecedent-law baseline and are not precedents for one another.

## Participation, law entering, and scope

All nine sitting Justices participated at argument and decision: {ALL_NAMES}. No recusal or other participation limitation is identified. Nine participants supply a quorum and five votes suffice for a Court proposition. Review is by certiorari under the supplied merits posture. The law-entering reading slice is `../entering-law/OT_2002CHUNK3_B.md`, derived from the opening authorities plus the effective public rules of Ventura and Bean where relevant. Governing propositions, unchanged authority, actual application, and nonreach grounds are set out in the identical internal and public Holdings sections below. Later and uncompleted cases supply no law.

## Stone: approved core and final compatibility

{case['stone_audit']}

### Approved Section II, copied mechanically

{extract_case(stone,case['number'])}

## Public action, judgment, and remedy

{case['judgment']}

## Opinion form, opinion table, and assignment

**Form fixed before counting:** {case['fixed_opinion_form']}

{internal_opinion_table}

**Assignment:** @@ASSIGNMENT@@

## Controlling holdings

{case['holdings']}

## Precedent and current law

{case['precedent']}

{case['law']}

## Continuity and post-action procedure

{case['procedure']}

The roster, circuit allotments, and standing practices are unchanged. This Supreme Court merits event is complete when validated and committed; ordinary lower-court proceedings are not an open Supreme Court application. No later filing, judgment, legislative response, or institutional action is admitted.

### Published noncontrolling positions retained for continuity

{case['separates'] or 'No separate opinion is published.'}

## Adaptive audit annex

### Frozen reconciled positions and historical comparison, copied mechanically

{extract_case(reconciled,case['number'])}

### Final proposition and disposition compatibility

{case['compatibility']}

{case.get('departure','')}

No modeled Associate changes commitment during assembly. Each exact join is stated in the opinion table and the authority for each holding; judgment agreement alone is not treated as a full rationale join. There is a direct majority for every controlling proposition and no Marks synthesis.

## Sources, limitations, and validation

Research cutoff: {case['date']}. The neutral packet and addendum support the objective posture, material record, questions, and statute; the entering-law slice supplies actual governing law. The frozen reconciliation supplies each Associate’s ground, full primary-comparator reading receipt, and explicit reconciliation changes. The approved Section II above controls Stone. Original petitions, complete party briefs, and joint appendices were not independently read in this assembly, and no missing source is treated as litigant omission. No additional reconstruction premise or new factual finding is introduced.

Source artifacts: `../freeze/OT_2002CHUNK3_B_NEUTRAL.md`; `../freeze/OT_2002CHUNK3_B_NEUTRAL_ADDENDUM.md`; `../freeze/OT_2002CHUNK3_B_RECONCILED.md`; `../runtime/OT_2002CHUNK3_B_STONE.md`; the case’s saved syllabus in `../research/chunk3-control/`. Eldred additionally uses only the Eldred paragraph of the fresh neutral addendum; Recio additionally uses `../freeze/OT_2002CHUNK3_RECIO_VALIDATED_NEUTRAL.md`, which preserves the exact source-extracted procedural supplement and fresh validation under Engine §14(2). Source Notes below contain public citations and judicial-record limits only.

The draft was constructed with one shared Holdings string for the internal and public sections; the local check verifies identity, the eleven-block sequence, explanation ceilings, complete nine-Justice component accounting, and the intended placeholders. Assignment counts, final lead author, canonical promotion, and term-wide validation are deliberately pending root assembly and are not certified as complete here.

**Validation status:** @@VALIDATION@@

## Public Projection

'''
    output = internal + '\n\n'.join('## '+block+'\n\n'+public[block] for block in BLOCKS) + '\n'
    (OUT / case['filename']).write_text(output,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
    projection = output.split('## Public Projection\n\n',1)[1]
    assert re.findall(r'(?m)^## (.+)$',projection) == BLOCKS
    internal_h = output.split('## Controlling holdings\n\n',1)[1].split('\n\n## Precedent and current law',1)[0]
    public_h = projection.split('## Holdings\n\n',1)[1].split('\n\n## Precedent Treatment',1)[0]
    assert internal_h == public_h
    forbidden = ['file://','simulation','approval','@@ASSIGNMENT@@','@@VALIDATION@@']
    assert not any(term in projection for term in forbidden)
    metadata.append({key:case[key] for key in ['filename','case','date','fixed_opinion_form','eligible_full_rationale_authors','full_joiners','componentvotes','fit_possible_authors']})
    metadata[-1]['tentativejudgment'] = case['result']
    metadata[-1]['assignment_authority'] = "O'Connor (most senior Associate in the affirmance coalition)" if case['number']==35 else 'Chief Justice Stone-Zsela'
    metadata[-1]['partial_joins'] = {'Stone-Zsela':['II-A']} if case['number']==35 else ({'Stone-Zsela':['I','III'],'Stevens':['I']} if case['number']==38 else {})
    print(case['filename'],len(output.split()),'words; blocks/identity/arithmetic passed')

(ROOT / 'runtime/OT_2002CHUNK3_B_ASSEMBLY.json').write_text(json.dumps(metadata,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n',encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
